{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420388-m20-lesser-banishing-ritual-of-the-pentagram-rote","id":1420388,"title":"M20 - Lesser Banishing Ritual of the Pentagram Rote","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-26T19:50:32-07:00","id":1420388,"title":"M20 - Lesser Banishing Ritual of the Pentagram Rote","content":"For those who don't know, the LBRP is a classic banishing ritual used by the Order of the Golden Dawn and many occultists since. I would presume that in M20 sphere terms it is Spirit 3; I can also look up what to recite, but I just want to ask what the gameplay would be. You know, the lore piece is very important, but the actual mechanics of the spell are very important too.<br /> <br /> For example, would it be a ritual that thickens and thins the Gauntlet, then attacks any minor demons who remain? What would a &quot;banishing&quot; ritual be in gameplay terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T21:10:11-07:00","id":1420399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420388-m20-lesser-banishing-ritual-of-the-pentagram-rote#post1420388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, would it be a ritual that thickens and thins the Gauntlet, then attacks any minor demons who remain? What would a &quot;banishing&quot; ritual be in gameplay terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is protective, it is either self-targeted or focused on the area of the pentagram, keeping evil things out, past the chalk line (chalk, blood, ink, salt, whatever it might be). The gauntlet bars entry into the world by Umbrood, regardless if they are good or evil. You could say that Spirits regarded as good by the mage's paradigm are in tune with the Resonance he has established through Magickal practice. This way, using personal resonance as the determining factor, you do not need Mind to determine the spirit's intent or inclination. <br /> <br /> Spheres: Spirit 3, Lull Spirit - &quot;there is nothing of interest inside this circle&quot;. As ST, I would allow a Shallowing to stay open for friendly Umbrood aligned with personal resonance. If it's more like a force field, add Forces. <br /> <br /> What if the Mage is in the Umbra already, where the Umbrood is in its own domain? Spirit 4, Bind Spirit - compel it to remain outside the circle forever. Spirit 5 Forge Ephemera - make a metaphysical barrier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T16:14:27-07:00","id":1420726,"title":"","content":"I would argue that LBRP is so ubiquitous as to be a background aspect of magical practice. Less Effect than Instrument (or at least part of their repertoire of gestures and intonations). Employed as part of every ritual, regardless of Effect, as part of best practices. (If a character botches a ritual, the player/ST might rationalize it as being the PC's failure to enact the LBRP and the resulting corruption of their magickal working).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can absolutely see it as being used by itself. Probably less for a specific Effect, and more as an Instrument for a variety of related but distinct Effects. Not unlike how a Hermetic may employ a crystal ball with Time to see into the past or future, or with Correspondence to see a distant location, or Mind to peer into someone's dreams. The tool is the same, but its application is contextual. Spirit 2 to increase the local Gauntlet rating, making it harder for spirits to affect the material world. Spirit 3 to outright rebuke meddlesome spirits. Prime may be employed as part of Countermagic/Antimagic, or at higher levels to nullify Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T22:18:55-07:00","id":1420771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420388-m20-lesser-banishing-ritual-of-the-pentagram-rote?p=1420726#post1420726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that LBRP is so ubiquitous as to be a background aspect of magical practice. Less Effect than Instrument (or at least part of their repertoire of gestures and intonations). Employed as part of every ritual, regardless of Effect, as part of best practices. (If a character botches a ritual, the player/ST might rationalize it as being the PC's failure to enact the LBRP and the resulting corruption of their magickal working).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can absolutely see it as being used by itself. Probably less for a specific Effect, and more as an Instrument for a variety of related but distinct Effects. Not unlike how a Hermetic may employ a crystal ball with Time to see into the past or future, or with Correspondence to see a distant location, or Mind to peer into someone's dreams. The tool is the same, but its application is contextual. Spirit 2 to increase the local Gauntlet rating, making it harder for spirits to affect the material world. Spirit 3 to outright rebuke meddlesome spirits. Prime may be employed as part of Countermagic/Antimagic, or at higher levels to nullify Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, sort of like how &quot;group rites&quot; is listed as a possible instrument, this rite would be an Instrument in as part of a larger ritual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}